    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0236" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/3477: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stafford</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-03T18:00:00-04:00">September 3, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Upon study of President Trujillo’s Note and Plan we feel there are going to
                    be insuperable objections to the plan as stated, but we <pb facs="0237" n="117"
                        xml:id="pg117"/> are making strenuous efforts to find constructive solution.
                    We have stated to Despradel<anchor n="28" xml:id="d122-f1"/> today and request
                    that you state to Dunn and President Trujillo our conviction that immediate
                    passage of law proposed in Trujillo’s Plan would prejudice constructive solution
                    of problem which probably will require cooperation New York bankers. Please
                    strongly urge delay in passage of law and urge that Dunn come to Washington by
                    airplane to confer Schoenfeld<anchor n="29" xml:id="d122-f2"/> and Department
                    next Wednesday if possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d122-f1" n="28" xml:id="d122-f1-content">
                <p>Roberto Despradel, Dominican Minister at Washington.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d122-f2" n="29" xml:id="d122-f2-content">
                <p>H. F. Arthur Schoenfeld, appointed Minister to the Dominican Republic. He
                    presented his letter of credence on October 9.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
